<%#
  THE README EDITOR (stage 4, S4-4; story 5.3). Mounted inside BOTH cards' `.readme` region —
  projects/_readme_card for a plain folder, projects/_repo_card for a folder that IS a working
  tree — so a maker writes documentation the same way whichever shape their project has.

  Locals: project, row (the README's Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Row, or nil when there is none).
  Optional — A REFUSED SAVE (2026-11-02, the UX audit's B3; Projects::ReadmesController): draft (the
  text that was posted), base_token (the token it was posted with), error, open.

  CLOSED, AND LAZY (the modelviewer `lazy` argument): readme_controller.js fetches the README's
  bytes on the first toggle-open and not before, so a project page nobody edits pays no port read
  at all and page_query_budget_test.rb is untouched by this feature.

  THE TEXTAREA AND THE BUTTON START DISABLED WHEN THERE IS A README TO FETCH, and are enabled by
  the controller once the buffer holds the real bytes. Without that, a failed bundle load plus a
  click on Save posts an EMPTY buffer over a README that took an hour to write. The server refuses
  a blank body as well (Projects::ReadmesController) — two halves, because a rule that lives only
  in JavaScript is one curl walks past, which is the same argument FilesController::EDITABLE_MAX_BYTES
  already makes. With NO README both start live: the textarea already holds the template, there
  is nothing a blank submit could destroy, and a disabled control is DROPPED from a submission —
  so this is also what lets "Write a README" work with no JavaScript at all.

  A DRAFT IS THE BUFFER, NOT THE FILE. A refused save renders this partial with what the maker
  typed in the textarea, live from the start, and `data-readme-draft-value` tells the controller
  not to fetch: fetching would overwrite the draft with the very bytes it was refused against.
  The token is the one the draft was POSTED with, so saving it again over a README that moved is
  refused again rather than quietly winning; the error says how to see the current version.

  PLAIN TAG HELPERS, NOT `f.text_area`. `form_with url:` with no model has a blank object_name, and
  a field built through the builder would be named "content" anyway — but `fields_for` on a blank
  object_name emits the literal bracket key Rack cannot parse (§14d, shipped twice). Flat names,
  read as params[:content] / params[:base_token], exactly as FilesController#update reads them.
%>
<% draft = local_assigns[:draft] %>
<% error = local_assigns[:error] %>
<% drafting = !draft.nil? %>
<details class="composer readme-editor" id="readme-editor" data-controller="readme" data-action="toggle->readme#reveal"
         data-readme-url-value="<%= row && !drafting ? blob_file_path(row.node_id) : "" %>"
         data-readme-draft-value="<%= drafting %>" <%= "open" if local_assigns[:open] %>>
  <summary class="btn small"><%= row ? "Edit README" : "Write a README" %></summary>
  <% if error.present? %>
    <div class="form-errors flash-alert composer-error" role="alert">
      <%= error %>
      <% if row %><%= link_to "Open the current README", file_path(row.node_id), target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %><% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <% if row && !drafting %>
    <%# WITH JAVASCRIPT OFF AN EXISTING README SHOWS A DISABLED, EMPTY TEXTAREA — the bytes are
        fetched by readme_controller.js and the controls stay disabled until they arrive (a Save
        before that would blank the file). Silent is safe and still unkind, so say why. The
        no-README case needs no script: the template is in the textarea and the controls are live. %>
    <noscript><p class="muted">Editing this README needs JavaScript; without it the file can only be replaced from the Library.</p></noscript>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "shared/no_history_note" %>

  <%= form_with url: project_readme_path(project), method: :patch, class: "readme-form",
                data: { action: "submit->readme#sync" } do %>
    <% if drafting %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :base_token, local_assigns[:base_token] %>
    <% elsif row %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :base_token, FileLayer.current.stat(current_user, node_id: row.node_id)&.content_token %>
    <% end %>
    <div class="readme-mount" data-readme-target="mount"></div>
    <% locked = row.present? && !drafting %>
    <label class="label-hidden" for="readme-source">README text</label>
    <%= text_area_tag :content, (drafting ? draft : (row ? "" : Maker::Readme.template_for(project))),
                      id: "readme-source", rows: 16, disabled: locked, spellcheck: true,
                      class: "readme-source", data: { readme_target: "input" } %>
    <div class="readme-bar">
      <%= submit_tag "Save README", class: "btn small", disabled: locked,
                     data: { readme_target: "submit" } %>
      <span class="muted readme-status" data-readme-target="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</details>
